  "context": "## Piece Identity & Inventory Orchestration\nConnecting anti-counterfeiting, RFID, digital fingerprints and high-value piece movement.\n\nIn high-end luxury, managing physical pieces is not a simple inventory problem. It is a problem of trust, authenticity, logistics, client experience and operational choreography.\n\nThousands of references in production, tens of thousands of pieces circulating, and decades of historical production including rare and highly valuable pieces.\n\nPieces move across boutiques, vaults, repair centers, private events, rooms, trays and presentations, often under strict timing and scarcity constraints.\n\nFor an older or rare piece, the questions are immediate: Is it authentic? Has it been modified or tampered with? What is its history? Can a boutique seeing it for the first time provide a reliable answer quickly?\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 31.25%; Authority, permissions and delegation 12.50%; Minimum control and sufficiency 12.50%; Decisions and responsibility 18.75%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 12.50%; Transformation and operational continuity 12.50%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/piece-identity-inventory-orchestration-e1567/\nSource document: https://jubap.eu/luxury-piece-identity-dynamic-inventory-orchestration/\n\n",
